  "description": "Every now & then a bike comes along that just drops your jaw. Your friends’ eyes widen when they see you on it. You can’t quite explain it, but you feel instantly connected to this new shred mate. What is it about this bike? The balance? The way it stays planted while devouring everything in its path? The unmatched responsiveness and pop over roots, rocks, and lips? Or that audible BRAAP in corners? Maybe it’s the confidence it builds—fast—as you zip up climbs. It’s definitely all of the above. Careful now, a bike like this might tempt you to throw caution to the wind: ride everything, do nothing else. Eat, sleep, ride, repeat.\nThe Remote 160 CR is that bike. It rides like your carbon Process 153—with an engine that kicks like a mechanical horse. Its sleek carbon frame features a purposefully low center of gravity. The Bosch SX system is silky smooth, and the PowerMore range extender hugs the motor to keep weight balanced. The SX system adapts to your ride, while the flip chip lets you go MX today or match wheel sizes tomorrow. Saddle up. Ride it once—good luck going back.",
